The Dynamic Button driver's Button tab includes icons from four icon collections, listed
below with their licenses. They are stored as SVG path data in
drivers/dynamic_button/www/html/index.html:

- The included icons, written by tools/bundle_icons.py from the names in
  tools/bundled-icons.txt, unmodified apart from their color.
- The three icon packs, written by tools/icon_packs.py from resources/icon-packs. The
  Classic Tile and Modern pictures place the collections' symbols, kept in
  resources/icon-packs/glyphs with each collection's license file, on a tile or in a frame
  and color them. The Classic Device pictures in resources/icon-packs/classic-device are
  Finite Labs' own drawings, most built around a Material Design Icons symbol; the list in
  resources/icon-packs/subjects.tsv names the symbol each picture uses.

The driver carries these four notices, with the texts of the Apache License 2.0, the ISC
License and the MIT License, in
drivers/dynamic_button/www/LICENSES.txt.

